# The `tabula::ignore-heavy` fixture: a matrix that is mostly nothing.
#
# 15 of 20 cells IGNORE, which is 75% against `ignoreHeavyPercent` (70). The
# lint's point is that such a machine is usually several machines wearing one
# name -- each state answers one action and ignores the rest.
#
# The shape is forced, which is worth recording. Every row needs a non-IGNORE
# cell or `dead-row` fires, and every column needs one or `dead-column` does,
# so with N states and M actions the most IGNORE a clean matrix can hold is
# roughly (M-1)/M. Three actions caps out at 66% and cannot reach the
# threshold at all; five actions reach 75%. That is why this fixture is 4x5
# while every other one is 3x3.
#
# Quiet elsewhere: each row has a HANDLE or a GO, no column is all IGNORE, a
# HANDLE means the matrix is not fully static so `no-static-entry` is gated
# off, no UNREACHABLE cells, and no payloads at all.

machine Poll
initial Idle
states  Idle Armed Firing Spent
actions Arm Tick Fire Reset Abort

Idle   | HANDLE | IGNORE | IGNORE | IGNORE   | IGNORE
Armed  | IGNORE | HANDLE | IGNORE | IGNORE   | GO(Idle)
Firing | IGNORE | IGNORE | HANDLE | IGNORE   | IGNORE
Spent  | IGNORE | IGNORE | IGNORE | GO(Idle) | IGNORE
